# Normalise line endings: LF in the repository and in working copies on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks files out as CRLF,
# the mixed-line-ending hook added in .pre-commit-config.yaml rewrites them all
# back to LF on the first run after every fresh clone, and they then show up as
# modified even though `git diff` reports no content change at all. Pinning
# eol=lf makes that hook a genuine no-op instead.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never munge binaries. text=auto detects most of these anyway; listing the
# ones a blog package is likely to grow makes it explicit.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
